"comparison": "Both C and MS disclose specific FICO score quality metrics for distinct consumer lending portfolios. C reports that its U.S. Retail Services portfolio FICO distribution was 'broadly stable quarter-over-quarter and year-over-year' reflecting 'strong underlying credit quality' (c_2024_7_P335_S001, c_2024_7_P335_S002). Similarly, MS reports that for its Wealth Management residential real estate loans, 'more than 75%... were to borrowers with \"Exceptional\" or \"Very Good\" FICO scores (i.e., exceeding 740)' as of year-end 2024 (ms_2024_7_P361_S001). Both disclosures use FICO scores to substantiate the credit quality of their respective consumer-facing portfolios, although C emphasizes stability over time while MS emphasizes the high percentage of high-score borrowers at a specific point in time.",
